cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the derived data, please cite both the software and the paper it supports."
title: "Analysis code for: Can ISC Bulletin Focal Depths Resolve Seismicity Relative to the Hormuz Detachment? Evidence from Reporting Agencies and Network Geometry in the Fars Arc, Zagros"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Khalili
    given-names: Marzieh
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9524-5347"
    email: marzieh-khalili@shirazu.ac.ir
    affiliation: "Department of Earth Sciences, College of Sciences, Shiraz University, Shiraz, Iran"
  - family-names: Fotoohi
    given-names: Ali
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering and IT, Faculty of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Shiraz University, Shiraz, Iran"
keywords:
  - seismology
  - earthquake catalog
  - focal depth
  - azimuthal gap
  - network geometry
  - Zagros
  - Fars Arc
  - ISC Bulletin
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis of International Seismological Centre Bulletin arrival
  and origin data for the Fars Arc of the Zagros fold and thrust belt. The code
  quantifies the quantization of the reported depth column, the dependence of
  pooled depth statistics on the mix of reporting agencies, the azimuthal gap
  recomputed at a series of epicentral-distance cutoffs, and the fraction of
  events whose recording geometry can constrain focal depth.
